What this covers
----------------

  data/     the sourced mythology layer — characters, relations, stories,
            places and lineages, the cultural-legacy records, the geographic
            data, and the generated indexes built from them.
  docs/     the research catalogs and planning documents — SOURCES.md,
            CHARACTERS.md, CONTRADICTIONS.md, the dynasty dossiers, PLAN.md
            and the feature plans.

Source code is under the MIT License (see LICENSE); audio is all rights
reserved. LICENSING.md at the repository root gives the whole picture.


Why ShareAlike
--------------

This is not only a preference. Part of the material is derived from sources
that are themselves ShareAlike:

  - data/reference/*.json adapts Wikipedia articles (CC BY-SA 4.0); each file
    carries its own `attribution` string naming the article.
  - data/geo/basemap.json adapts a Wikimedia Commons SVG map series
    (CC BY-SA 3.0).

That material cannot be relicensed under permissive terms by anyone,
including the copyright holder of the surrounding work. Downstream users
inherit the same obligation.

Some parts carry additional upstream terms that travel with them — notably
river geometry derived from OpenStreetMap, which is licensed under the Open
Database License (ODbL 1.0) and remains so regardless of this file.
ATTRIBUTION.md lists every upstream source, its license, and what was taken.


How to attribute
----------------

A reasonable credit for the work as a whole:

  "Icarus Atlas" by Mehmet Fatih Aksoy, CC BY-SA 4.0
  https://github.com/e7hdk/icarus-atlas

If you reuse a specific fact, keep its `sources` and `citation` fields with
it. They are the point of the dataset: every mythological claim records which
ancient authors attest it, and stripping that turns sourced research back
into unattributed assertion.


What is not here
----------------

The ancient primary texts are not redistributed in this repository.
research/corpus/manifest.json pins their editions, URLs, licenses and
checksums; `pnpm corpus:sync` fetches them into a gitignored local corpus.
Their licenses are the originators' own — see ATTRIBUTION.md.
